## Enforcement

Mechanical checks back the rules above. When a check fails, fix the code. Never disable or loosen the check.

| Rule | Enforced by |
| --- | --- |
| Module encapsulation | {{BOUNDARY_ENFORCEMENT}} |
| Exhaustive handling of domain ADTs | {{ADT_ENFORCEMENT}} |
| Interface comments on public declarations | {{INTERFACE_COMMENT_ENFORCEMENT}} |
| Boundary types and validation | {{VALIDATOR}}, via `{{CMD_CHECK}}` |
| Wire contracts | {{CONTRACT_CHECKS}}, via `{{CMD_CHECK}}` |
| Behavior and invariants | {{BDD_TOOL}} and {{PBT_TOOL}}, via `{{CMD_TEST}}` |
| Test strength | {{MUTATION_TOOL}}, via `{{CMD_MUTATION}}` |
